          "title": "You'll want to know: cotillear",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "cotillear — \"to gossip\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Mis vecinas cotillean en la escalera. My neighbours gossip on the stairs."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Spain; a gossip is un cotilla. In Latin America people say chismear."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "cotillear is built on cotilla \"a gossip\" with the ending -ear. For cotilla in this sense the origin is not settled; an older cotilla was a corset."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
